# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Publish policy: only what is needed to RUN the application, models included.
#
# Runtime needs exactly three model files (~640 MB total):
#   checkpoints/blip_large_head/best.pt    544 MB  the captioner
#   checkpoints/quality_gate/best.pt         2 MB  the quality gate
#   checkpoints/easyocr/*.pth               94 MB  OCR (optional, see below)
#
# Everything else on disk is training input or training output. The feature
# caches alone are 140 GB and are all regenerable, so none of it is published.
#
# The BLIP weights themselves are NOT in this repo: `transformers` downloads
# `Salesforce/blip-image-captioning-large` into the Hugging Face cache on first
# run. That is why checkpoints/*/best.pt is 544 MB rather than ~1.8 GB.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Virtual environments ---------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Downloaded datasets and derived caches (140 GB, all regenerable) -------
data/raw/
data/features/
data/interim/
data/processed/

# Manifests are image/caption *indexes* - they hold filenames and captions, not
# the images themselves. Only the VizWiz set is published, because that is the
# domain the app actually runs on. The COCO and Flickr30k manifests belong to an
# approach that was measured and abandoned (see train/docs/captioner-experiments.md)
# and are ~111 MB of dead weight.
data/manifests/*
!data/manifests/vizwiz_val.jsonl
!data/manifests/vizwiz_test.jsonl
!data/manifests/vizwiz_train.jsonl

# --- Training outputs -------------------------------------------------------
# Every checkpoint except the two the app loads. `last.pt` is a resume file
# (~1.6 GB for BLIP-large) and is not needed to run anything.
checkpoints/*
!checkpoints/blip_large_head/
!checkpoints/quality_gate/
!checkpoints/easyocr/
checkpoints/*/last.pt
checkpoints/*/epoch_*.pt
checkpoints/*/vocab.pkl

# Run outputs: configs, per-epoch metrics, prediction logs. Large and not
# needed at runtime. The one exception is the run_config.json the captioner
# reads to learn its tune mode - that lives under checkpoints/, not here.
runs/

# --- Working directories ----------------------------------------------------
.tmp/
.tools/
.archive/

# --- Scratch and scratch-like artefacts at the root -------------------------
# Proposal drafts, screenshots, scratch files. Not part of the application.
*.docx
*.webp
*.zip
com.jpg
images.jpg
jess.jpg
py

# Proposal and design artefacts: an HTML prototype, rendered document previews,
# and proposal drafts. Kept locally, not part of running the app. The written
# docs under train/docs/ ARE published - they are small and explain how the
# system works.
prototype/
preview-v2e/
preview-dataset-v6/
dataset-stats.json
build_proposal_v2.py
concept-proposal-v2.md

# --- Editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT ignored on purpose:
#   train/**                     the backend itself
#   train/configs/ocr_frozen.json  runtime config for --ocr
#   data/manifests/*.jsonl       image/caption lists the app reads
#   tools/android-env.ps1        build helper for the Flutter app
#   FrontEnd Submission/**       the Flutter source (its own .gitignore already
#                                excludes build/ and .dart_tool/)
#
# OCR is currently disabled by default in train/serve.py. Its weights are still
# published so `--ocr` works without a download; to drop them instead, add:
#   checkpoints/easyocr/
# They are re-downloaded on first use into the same directory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
